   1 │ # Ports
   2 │ 
   3 │ Supported, official, or officially acknowledged ports for the Spine data format.
   4 │ 
   5 │ | Language | Library Name   | Status   |
   6 │ |----------|----------------|----------|
   7 │ | Rust     | `spinelib`     | Unstable |
   8 │ 
   9 │ _(that's it currently...)_
  10 │ 
  11 │ _(yes not even a C port even though the spine-c header exists, that's not an official port by my standards)_
  12 │ 
  13 │ ---
  14 │ 
  15 │ # Contributing
  16 │ 
  17 │ ## Overview
  18 │ 
  19 │ `spine-c` exposes the official C ABI for creating bindings to other languages.
  20 │ 
  21 │ Bindings should target:
  22 │ - `include/spine.h`
  23 │ - the generated shared libraries
  24 │ 
  25 │ ## Supported library formats
  26 │ 
  27 │ - Linux/BSD: `.so`
  28 │ - Windows: `.dll`
  29 │ - macOS: `.dylib`
  30 │ 
  31 │ ## CI artifacts
  32 │ 
  33 │ Prebuilt libraries are available from GitHub Actions artifacts/releases.
